Let $R$ be a Noetherian commutative ring and $\mathbb{T} = (S^{1})^{\times r}$ a torus of rank $r$. The tt-category $\mathrm{Mod}(R^{h\mathbb{T}})$ is stratified over the graded affine space
\begin{equation}
\mathrm{Spc}(\mathrm{Mod}^c(R^{h\mathbb{T}})) \cong \mathrm{Spec}^h(\pi_*R^{h\mathbb{T}}) \cong \mathrm{Spec}^h(R[x_1,\ldots,x_r]),
\end{equation}
where $|x_i|=-2$ for all $i$.

Let $G$ be a finite group and $R$ a regular commutative ring. Cohomological support induces  bijections 
\[
\begin{Bmatrix}
\text{Non-zero localizing tensor } \\
\text{ideals of } \cat \mathrm{Lat}(G,R)
\end{Bmatrix} 
\xymatrix@C=2pc{ \ar[r]^-{\sim} &}
\begin{Bmatrix}
\text{Subsets of}  \\
\mathrm{Proj}(H^*(G;R))
\end{Bmatrix}
\]
and
\[
\begin{Bmatrix}
\text{Non-zero thick} \\
\text{ideals of } \cat \mathrm{lat}(G,R)
\end{Bmatrix} 
\xymatrix@C=2pc{ \ar[r]^-{\sim} &}
\begin{Bmatrix}
\text{Specialization closed}  \\
\text{subsets of } \mathrm{Proj}(H^*(G;R))
\end{Bmatrix}.
\]
